# TODO - Custom target profile identity

## Objective

Allow user-supplied target profiles with canonical hashing and explicit artifact
identity. Investigate profile-dependent encoding without making a false claim
that reverse engineering can be made cryptographically impossible.


**Current implementation.**

- `malbolge-profile-v1` canonicalizes profile ID, version, target schema,
  word/memory geometry, and semantics to compact sorted ASCII JSON, then binds
  those bytes with a self-describing SHA-256 fingerprint.
- Registry `kind` is deliberately excluded so a published profile keeps the
  same fingerprint when its lifecycle role changes from current to versioned.
<!-- jig-ignore-next-line: canonical path or identifier is indivisible -->
- `src/interoperability/profile-compatibility/contract/profile-fingerprints.json`
  and `src/runtime/virtual-machine/contract/profile_generated.rs`
  are deterministic generated projections; tests require byte-exact renderer
  equality, and Rust exposes the fingerprint through `ProfileDescriptor`.
- External schema-v1 custom profiles omit registry `kind`, preserve the defining
  Malbolge semantic core, and may not redefine an existing canonical profile ID
  with different content.
- `.\.dependencies\python\3.14.6\Scripts\python-jig.cmd -m
  scripts.validate.profile_identity` prints or verifies fingerprints.
  Mismatch uses stable code `MALBOLGE-PROFILE-ID-001` with expected/observed
  identities and never silently substitutes another configuration.
- Experiment Manifest v1 now requires exact generated fingerprints for
  canonical target IDs, rejects stale hashes with `MALBOLGE-PROFILE-ID-001`,
  rejects unknown IDs without fallback, and forbids fingerprints on aggregate
  research scopes. Ten checked-in manifests carry the binding.
- The `MALBCAP1` runtime capsule also carries the canonical ID/fingerprint pair,
  emits the shared expected/observed mismatch diagnostic after valid-checksum
  tampering, and rejects unknown profile IDs without fallback before payload
  use.
- Portable effect IR v3 and native cache keys retain exact profile ID and
  fingerprint plus canonical version/features/geometry. Direct
  x86-64/AArch64 COFF objects embed the same envelope in versioned read-only
  `.mbprof` metadata; structural admission rejects absence, tampering, or
  object/key mismatch before semantic admission.
- SHA-256 is used for identity/integrity only; no secrecy or anti-reverse-
  engineering claim is made. Bootstrap compiler-object and product artifact
  propagation remain open.

## Acceptance

- Generated artifacts bind to a canonical profile fingerprint; supplying a
  nonmatching external configuration is detected rather than silently
  interpreted under different semantics.
- `malbolge-1998` preserves defined original-interpreter semantics;
  current-language
  behavior and capacity are gated by explicit versioned profile identity.
- The declared scope contains no unresolved placeholder implementation or
  undocumented workaround required for this objective to function.
- Evidence is durable enough to move this TODO to `docs/todo/completed/` and
  remove the exact TODO heading without losing unfinished intent.

